  "starterCode": "# Decoupled RoPE — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(content, positional, positions, theta=10000.0):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Decoupled RoPE** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(content, positional, positions, theta=10000.0):\n    # Content channels pass through; the separate positional subvector receives RoPE.\n    x=np.asarray(positional,dtype=float); pos=np.asarray(positions,dtype=float); dim=x.shape[-1]\n    if dim%2: raise ValueError(\"positional dimension must be even\")\n    inv=1.0/(theta**(np.arange(0,dim,2,dtype=float)/dim)); ang=pos[...,None]*inv\n    c,s=np.cos(ang),np.sin(ang); y=np.empty_like(x)\n    y[...,0::2]=x[...,0::2]*c-x[...,1::2]*s; y[...,1::2]=x[...,0::2]*s+x[...,1::2]*c\n    return {\"content\":np.asarray(content,dtype=float).tolist(),\"positional\":y.tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
